<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Sept consumer prices up 9.83 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Sept consumer prices up 9.83 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's consumer price index rose 9.83 percent in September year-on-year, compared to 9.54 percent in August and 12.49 percent in September 1995, the Federal Bureau of Statistics said on Sunday.  </p>
<p>The index, using 1990/91 as base year, rose 1.16 percent to 181.99 in September after rising 1.3 percent in August to 179.9. The index stood at 325.92 in September 1995, when it was calculated using 1980/81 as base year.</p>
<p>					  Sept	Aug	  Sept 1995*</p>
<p>CONSUMER PRICE  base 1990/91   181.99    179.90	 325.92</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		  +1.16    +1.30	  +1.02</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		    +9.83    +9.54	  +12.49</p>
<p>* base 1980/81</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
